WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.641
-Well, my new poll numbers are
in, and it's not looking good.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.010
There's only one thing
left to do --

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.646
make cold calls
to normal, everyday Americans

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.584
and try to win back
their support.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.619
[ Line ringing ]

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:26.326
Congratulations,
you're speaking to Donald Trump.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.294
I'm calling undecided voters

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.863
who are way less rich
and way less successful than me.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:34.400
What poor loser
am I speaking to?

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.003
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.278
-Mike Bloomberg.

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:47.547
-Wait a second.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.349
The Michael Bloomberg of
Bloomberg News and Bloomberg TV?

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:51.551
-That's right.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.319
-And "Bloomberg Med"
and "Chicago Bloomberg"

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.889
and "Bloomberg 3: Tokyo Drift"?

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.624
-Sure, Donald.
-Well, this is fantastic.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.159
I was gonna ask you
for your vote,

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.628
but now that I have you
on the phone,

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.563
how about I just ask you some
questions like an interview?

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:06.966
Even a stable genius like me
would like to pick

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:11.671
Mike Bloomberg's very smart,
very huge brain.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.841
-You know I'm running
against you, right?

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.643
-Like I said -- very dumb brain.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.980
It's a teeny-tiny,
very small brain.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.715
Okay, let's get started --

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.918
Why exactly are you running
for president?

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.151
-Well, I've joined the race

00:01:26.151 --> 00:01:29.455
to return our country to sanity
and honesty...

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.958
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:39.231
...so we can be proud
of America again,

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:43.736
and step one is giving you
a New York goodbye.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.838
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.540
-Whoa. Whoa. Whoa. Whoa. Whoa.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.775
What's a New York goodbye?

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.345
-Sending you back to Queens
in a Yellow Cab

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.047
while Times Square Elmo
flips you off.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:58.851
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:03.923
-Wow. That's very mean, Mike.
Very mean. Very nasty.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.492
Very nasty. Very nasty answer.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:09.929
Didn't expect that from you.
Very, very nasty.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.564
Next question --
What makes you think

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.199
you'd be a better president
than me?

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.901
And you can't cheat
and use facts.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.536
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:19.305
-Well, let's see --
I'm a self-made businessman,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:22.208
a proven leader,
and a New York icon,

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.277
whereas you just play
those things on TV.

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:28.114
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.054
Plus, I was mayor
of the greatest city in America

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.757
with the greatest audience
in the world.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.026
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:46.499
-Well, I do love
New York City mayors.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.602
I even keep one as a pet.
Good boy.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.438
Good boy. Good boy.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.040
But, anyway, this is
the big leagues, Mike,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.276
the bigly big leagues,
so let me ask --

00:02:57.276 --> 00:03:00.245
What would you do if you got
to sit where I'm sitting?

00:03:00.245 --> 00:03:03.549
-Well, first, I'd wipe
the KFC grease off the seat...

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.551
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:10.256
...maybe take some of those
Kid Rock posters off the walls,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:13.792
and then I'd tackle key issues
like climate change

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:16.662
and gun safety
and income inequality...

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:20.800
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.470
...which would mean
raising taxes on billionaires.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.039
-Wait. I'm gonna have to pay
more in taxes?

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.041
-No, I said billionaires.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:33.813
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.514
-That was a low blow, Mike.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.716
I'm actually a very successful
person just like you.

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:40.152
I've created and run
many beautiful businesses,

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:43.088
and none of them have failed...

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:44.656
besides the casinos.

00:03:44.656 --> 00:03:46.592
-And the university?
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.261
-And the magazine.
-That's right.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.962
-And the steaks.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:51.831
-And the water.
-Forgot about that one.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.532
-And the board game.
-I did that?

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.134
-And the vodka.
-Pour one out.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.602
-And the airline.
-Okay! Okay! Okay!

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.170
Let's change the subject!
I don't like this.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.939
I don't like this game.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:04.009
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:07.446
Here's one more very perfect,
very important question --

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.815
Are you watching the Super Bowl
this weekend?

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:13.552
-Yes, I am. Actually,
I have a 60-second commercial

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.721
airing during the game.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:18.558
-Really? Me, too.
What's yours about?

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:22.261
-It's about an important issue
facing our country right now

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:25.497
and how I can use my experience
as a mayor and business leader

00:04:25.497 --> 00:04:27.266
to bring America forward.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:28.868
-Cool.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.170
In my commercial, I get really
angry, then I eat a Snickers bar

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.638
and turn into Betty White.

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:36.408
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:40.446
-Well, it's been a fun
interview, "Mini" Mike.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.549
That's my nickname for you,
by the way, Mini Mike.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.451
Do you have
any nicknames for me?

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:48.821
-Well, usually,
I just call you that [bleep].

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.089
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.490
-Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Stop that!
I've heard enough.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.858
I've heard enough.

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:55.661
I guess you learn a lot of
colorful words in New York City.

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.029
Rudy! No! Rudy!

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.797
I got to go, Mike.
Rudy just peed on the carpet.

00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:01.868
No, Rudy! Bad boy! Rudy!

